# Folder 41: an étale scheme of geometric irreducible components, not stated

The open row `41-irreducible-components-etale-criterion` of the edition's list of findings
(`src/content/findings.ts`), folder 41, pp. 3, 8–10. It is not stated; why.

* `41-irreducible-components-etale-criterion`: for `f : X → Y` of finite type, locally
  universally open and quasi-finite over an affine space at the generic points of the components
  of the fibres, an étale separated `Y`-scheme `M` whose geometric points over `y` index the
  geometrically irreducible components of `X_ȳ` exists if and only if, over every trait, no
  component of the generic fibre specialises to two components of the special fibre and
  distinct components do not meet in one specialisation; `M` is finite iff every generic
  component specialises. Status: unsearched. Not stated because the statement is not legible:
  the theorem's first condition is illegible, condition (iii) of p. 8 survives in fragments, the
  hypotheses on the trait are fragments, and the index `n − 1` of the affine space is undefined
  on the leaf; the row asks first for a re-reading against the facsimile. The notions would be
  available (Stacks has geometric irreducible components over a field and their Galois orbits,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.fiber_irreducibleComponentsBaseChangeMap_eq_orbit`, Stacks 04KY), but
  stating the reading's reconstruction would fix a statement the edition has not settled.
